    lead:"Brazil is the largest sovereign power in South America and the central prize in the continent's competition for markets, technology, and diplomatic influence. Its state is shaped by <a href='getulio-vargas.html'>Vargas</a>, <a href='brazilian-national-developmentalism.html'>national developmentalism</a>, the <a href='brazilian-coup-1964.html'>1964 coup</a>, and the <a href='brazilian-political-opening.html'>1985 civilian transition</a>; economically it approaches the Latin system through Portugal while remaining politically independent.",
